    "body": "### Description\nWith the server-side TCP authentication enforcement merged, official clients (starting with `pynvim`) need to be updated to support the new secure handshake (Phase 4 of the token authentication plan).\n\nClients connecting via TCP should check for the presence of the `NVIM_TCP_TOKEN_FILE` environment variable. If it exists, the client must read the 32-byte token from the specified path and automatically send the `nvim_authenticate` payload as its very first request.\n\n### Example\n\n**Before (Vulnerable/Manual):**\n```python\n# Unauthenticated connection\nfrom pynvim import attach\nnvim = attach('tcp', address='127.0.0.1', port=6666)\n# If enforcement is active, the connection drops here\n```\n\n**After (Streamlined & Secure):**\n```python\nimport os\nfrom pynvim import attach\n\n# Client automatically reads the token and performs the handshake\nos.environ[\"NVIM_TCP_TOKEN_FILE\"] = \"/path/to/token\"\nnvim = attach('tcp', address='127.0.0.1', port=6666)\nnvim.command('echo \"Secure connection established\"')\n```\n",
